(a) A payload is a device or equipment carried by the UAV, which performs the mission assigned. The payload comprises all elements of the air vehicle that are not necessary for flight but are carried for the purpose of fulfilling specific mission objectives. It is assumed that a UAV System Type Certification Basis may be released for several payload configurations.
(b) Where a UAV System is designed to carry payloads, the integration and operation of those payloads must
  (1) not adversely affect the safe flight and control of the UAV;
  (2) be shown as electromagnetically compatible (EMC) with systems on board of the UAV;
  (3) meet safety objectives as provided in USAR.1309.

